/*
========================================================
        IMPORTANT POINTS TO REMEMBER
========================================================

1. if
   -> Used to execute code when a condition is true.

2. if-else
   -> Used when there are two possible blocks.

3. else-if ladder
   -> Used when there are multiple conditions.

4. Nested if-else
   -> An if/else statement inside another if/else.

5. switch
   -> Used for multiple fixed/case-based choices.

6. break
   -> Stops the switch or loop immediately.

7. default
   -> Executes when no switch case matches.

8. % (modulus)
   -> Gives the remainder.
   Example:
   10 % 2 = 0
   10 % 3 = 1

9. && (AND)
   -> All conditions must be true.

10. || (OR)
    -> At least one condition must be true.

11. ===
    -> Checks value and data type.

12. !==
    -> Checks whether value or data type is different.
*/


